\sbkpage\sect\pard\sectd\paperh16840\paperw11907\margl768\margr5327\margb360\margt489\pard\ri4\qj\fi0\sl-240\f00 \fs21{\fs21\charscalex106\b0\i0\ul0\f00 mantic night poetry, in a landscape of crosses "sparse per la funerea campagna," in the abandoned forgottenceme\f02 \-\f00 teries where the hungry dog wanders. \fs23\charscalex91\b In \fs21\charscalex106\b0 contrast, a passage follows where the pious customs, the beliefs, the supersti\f02 \-\f00 _tions connected with burials are rehearsed. There may be a tone of eighteenth-century didacticism but it is tempered by the fact that those elements have an obvious function in the generaI pattern of the poem. Concreteness is main\f02 \-\f00 tained also through frequent transition from the generaI to the paliicular, and through shifts in the sharpness of vision and in verbal tenses (" ... nè le città \fs22\charscalex83\i fur \fs21\charscalex106\i0 meste/ D'effi\f02 \-\f00 giati scheletri; le madri / \fs21\charscalex100\i Balzan \fs21\charscalex106\i0 nè sonni esterrèfatte ... "). \par}
\pard
\pard\li48\sb38\qj\fi480\sl-240\f00 \fs21{\fs21\charscalex106\b0\i0\ul0\f00 Through such shifts the poem progresses even gram\f02 \-\f00 matically toward the suggestion that the poet's outlook is above time; there is a great fluidity in time Ievels; the scope of the poem and the outlook of the speaker are progressively and imperceptibly widened. \par}
\pard
