\pard\li33\ri24\sb124\qj\fi480\sl-235\f00 \fs20{\fs20\charscalex105\b0\i0\ul0\f00 The function of the poet becomes the imaginative reali\f02 \-\f00 zation of a tradition; and his poetry does not align and descl'ibe the matel'ials of that tl'adition but l'athel' dl'ama\f02 \-\f00 tizes the experience, the awareness of it. For example, we have a l'e-intl'oduction of the early mode of address to a friend, now mentioned by his Gl'eek first name in an ama of almost mythical voyage: \par}
