\sbkpage\sect\pard\sectd\paperh16840\paperw11907\margl753\margr5360\margb360\margt547\pard\ri1\sb4\qj\fi0\sl-240\f00 \fs21{\fs21\charscalex106\b0\i0\ul0\f00 human affairs, in which harmony (the "armonia" which "vince di ~ille secoli il silenzio") has been achieved -in which poetic contemplation is possible. And the possibility for human affairs to become the object of that contempla\f02 \-\f00 tion is a test of their greatness. Homer then represents the final version of the \fs21\charscalex100\i vates \fs21\charscalex106\i0 image; and his outlook, though prepared by the generaI direction of the poem, provides its comprehensive and transcendent conclusion. The idea of the \fs21\charscalex100\i patria \fs21\charscalex106\i0 transcends that of any historical country and generally symbolizes the object; of allegiance, the motive of lives significantly lived, whether in triumph or in defeat. A key-word, an adjective which seems singularly well placed to express that outlook is \fs21\charscalex100\i fatati: \fs21\charscalex106\i0 the final destroyers of Ilium are the carriers of fate and are themselves fated, they are gathering their "ultimo trofeo" in glory and ca\f02 \-\f00 lamity. Although the sympathy may go, as usual, to the defeated Trojans (the Romantic patriotic hero is Hector) the point of view of the "sacro vate" is above both. \par}
\pard
\pard\li19\ri1\sb4\qj\fi489\sl-235\f00 \fs21{\fs21\charscalex106\b0\i0\ul0\f00 Consequently the final impression left by the poem as expression of "patrioti c Romanticism" is that its \fs21\charscalex100\i patria \fs21\charscalex106\i0 is a cultural \fs21\charscalex100\i contaminatio, \fs21\charscalex106\i0 in fact, an "invention." Looking back at the whole poem we realize that the poet has at\f02 \-\f00 tempted, with a conciseness probably unparalleled in the period, and in terms of the special taste, the cultural train\f02 \-\f00 ing, and the sensibility that were his own, to perform a synthesis which in very different ways presents itself in literary history when a conciliation is attempted between the personal, the "civic" and the mythical. \par}
\pard
